(window.STEP_DATA = window.STEP_DATA || {})[15] = {"n":15,"set":"B","level":"Intermediate","band":"B1 50% · B2 50%","sec":[{"id":"R","name":"Reading Comprehension","ar":"فهم المقروء","min":70,"from":1,"to":40,"g":[{"t":"Research stations in Antarctica","p":["Antarctica is the coldest, driest and windiest continent on Earth. Almost all of it is covered by ice that is, on average, nearly two kilometres thick. No country owns Antarctica, and it has no permanent population. Yet every year, thousands of scientists and support staff from around the world live and work there in research stations, studying everything from climate change to the origins of the universe.","The way Antarctica is governed is unusual. In 1959, twelve countries signed the Antarctic Treaty, which declared that the continent should be used only for peaceful purposes and for scientific research. Military activity and mining are banned, and countries agreed to share their scientific findings. Today, more than fifty countries have joined the treaty, and around seventy research stations operate on the continent, some only in summer and others all year round.","Life at a research station is very different from life at home. In winter, temperatures can fall below minus sixty degrees Celsius, and in many places the sun does not rise for weeks. Stations must be built to withstand extreme winds and heavy snow. Some modern stations stand on legs that can be raised, so that snow does not bury them. All food, fuel and equipment must be brought in by ship or plane, usually during the short summer, because the sea ice makes access almost impossible in winter.","Scientists in Antarctica carry out a wide range of research. By drilling deep into the ice, they extract ice cores: long cylinders of ice that contain tiny bubbles of ancient air. These bubbles allow scientists to measure the amount of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere hundreds of thousands of years ago, providing valuable information about how the climate has changed over time. Antarctica is also an excellent place for astronomy, because the air is dry and clear and there is very little light pollution. Biologists, meanwhile, study penguins, seals and microorganisms that survive in extreme conditions.","Living in such isolation can be psychologically challenging. During the long winter, small teams may spend months together with no way of leaving. Researchers have found that people can suffer from sleep problems, low mood and difficulties in relationships. To reduce these effects, stations organize regular social activities, maintain strict daily routines and provide gyms and special lights that imitate daylight. Space agencies study life in Antarctic stations to learn how astronauts might cope on long missions to Mars.","Human activity in Antarctica also brings environmental risks, such as pollution from fuel and waste. Under the treaty's environmental rules, almost all waste must be removed from the continent, and visitors must follow strict guidelines to avoid disturbing wildlife. The challenge is to continue valuable research while protecting one of the last great wildernesses on the planet."],"q":[{"n":1,"s":"What is the passage mainly about?","o":["the history of polar exploration","scientific life and research in Antarctica","how penguins survive the cold","the climate of Mars"],"k":1,"ty":"main idea","e":"The passage describes research stations, research and challenges.","h":"الحياة والبحث العلمي في القطب الجنوبي."},{"n":2,"s":"According to the Antarctic Treaty, what is Antarctica used for?","o":["mining and military training","tourism only","fishing and farming","peaceful purposes and scientific research"],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 2 explains this.","h":"الأغراض السلمية والبحث العلمي."},{"n":3,"s":"Why do some modern stations stand on raisable legs?","o":["to protect them from earthquakes","so that snow does not bury them","to make them warmer","to allow planes to land underneath"],"k":1,"ty":"purpose","e":"Paragraph 3 explains this.","h":"حتى لا يدفنها الثلج."},{"n":4,"s":"Why are supplies usually delivered in summer?","o":["Sea ice makes access very difficult in winter.","Ships are cheaper in summer.","Scientists only arrive in summer.","It is dark all summer."],"k":0,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 3 gives the reason.","h":"الجليد البحري يمنع الوصول شتاءً."},{"n":5,"s":"What are ice cores useful for?","o":["finding oil under the ice","providing drinking water","measuring carbon dioxide levels in the distant past","studying penguin behaviour"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"Bubbles of ancient air show past CO2 levels.","h":"قياس ثاني أكسيد الكربون قديمًا."},{"n":6,"s":"Why is Antarctica a good place for astronomy?","o":["It is closer to the stars.","There are many large telescopes.","The sun never sets.","The air is dry and clear with little light pollution."],"k":3,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 4 explains this.","h":"هواء جاف وصافٍ."},{"n":7,"s":"The word 'isolation' in paragraph 5 is closest in meaning to","o":["extreme cold","being separated from other people","darkness","hard work"],"k":1,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"Small teams cannot leave for months.","h":"العزلة."},{"n":8,"s":"Why do space agencies study life in Antarctic stations?","o":["to find a place to build rockets","to learn how astronauts might cope on long missions","to train penguins for space","to test new types of fuel"],"k":1,"ty":"purpose","e":"Paragraph 5 explains this.","h":"لفهم تأقلم رواد الفضاء."},{"n":9,"s":"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a way to reduce psychological problems?","o":["allowing staff to leave whenever they want","regular social activities","strict daily routines","lights that imitate daylight"],"k":0,"ty":"NOT / EXCEPT","e":"Leaving is not possible in winter.","h":"المغادرة غير ممكنة."},{"n":10,"s":"What does the writer suggest in the last paragraph?","o":["All research stations should close.","Tourists should replace scientists.","Waste can be left in Antarctica.","Research must continue without harming the environment."],"k":3,"ty":"summary / conclusion","e":"The challenge is to research while protecting the wilderness.","h":"البحث مع حماية البيئة."}]},{"t":"The history of anaesthesia","p":["Today, it is almost impossible to imagine having an operation without anaesthesia, the use of drugs to prevent pain during medical procedures. Yet until the mid-nineteenth century, surgery was a terrifying experience. Patients were fully awake while surgeons cut through skin, muscle and bone, and speed was considered the most important skill a surgeon could have. Some patients died from shock and pain, and many people chose to suffer from their illness rather than face an operation.","People had long searched for ways to reduce pain. In ancient times, doctors used plants such as the opium poppy and mandrake, as well as alcohol. Medieval Muslim physicians, including Ibn Sina and al-Zahrawi, described the use of sponges soaked in mixtures of plant extracts that patients inhaled before surgery. However, these methods were unreliable: too little had no effect, while too much could be fatal.","The modern era of anaesthesia began in the 1840s. In 1842, an American doctor, Crawford Long, used a gas called ether to remove a tumour from a patient's neck, but he did not publish his results until several years later. On 16 October 1846, a dentist named William Morton gave a public demonstration of ether anaesthesia at Massachusetts General Hospital in Boston. A surgeon removed a tumour from a patient's neck while the patient slept peacefully. When the patient woke, he said that he had felt no pain. News of the demonstration spread rapidly around the world.","Soon afterwards, another substance, chloroform, became popular, especially in Britain. It was easier to use than ether, which had an unpleasant smell and could catch fire. Chloroform became widely accepted after Queen Victoria used it during the birth of her eighth child in 1853. However, doctors gradually realized that chloroform could cause dangerous heart problems, and it was eventually replaced by safer drugs.","Anaesthesia transformed medicine. Without the need to work at extreme speed, surgeons could perform longer and more complex operations, such as operations on the abdomen, chest and brain. Combined with the introduction of antiseptics, which reduced infections, anaesthesia made surgery far safer.","Modern anaesthesia is highly sophisticated. Anaesthetists, doctors who specialize in this field, carefully choose and combine drugs for each patient and monitor breathing, heart rate, blood pressure and oxygen levels throughout the operation. Local anaesthetics numb only a small part of the body, allowing patients to stay awake for minor procedures, such as dental treatment. Thanks to these advances, millions of operations are carried out safely every day."],"q":[{"n":11,"s":"What was surgery like before the mid-nineteenth century?","o":["Operations were slow and comfortable.","Only dentists performed surgery.","Patients slept with the help of gas.","Patients were awake and felt great pain."],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 1 describes this.","h":"المرضى مستيقظون ويتألمون."},{"n":12,"s":"Why was speed considered so important for surgeons?","o":["Patients were awake and in pain.","Hospitals were very busy.","Anaesthesia wore off quickly.","Surgeons were paid by the hour."],"k":0,"ty":"inference","e":"Shorter operations meant less suffering.","h":"لتقليل المعاناة."},{"n":13,"s":"What was the problem with early methods of reducing pain?","o":["They were too expensive.","They were not allowed by law.","They were unreliable, and too much could be fatal.","They made patients too hungry."],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 2 explains this.","h":"غير موثوقة وخطرة."},{"n":14,"s":"Why is William Morton's demonstration important?","o":["It was the first use of opium.","It proved chloroform was dangerous.","It introduced antiseptics.","It publicly showed that ether could prevent pain during surgery."],"k":3,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"News spread rapidly around the world.","h":"عرض علني لفعالية الأثير."},{"n":15,"s":"Why did Crawford Long not receive much early recognition?","o":["His patient died.","He did not publish his results for several years.","He used chloroform instead of ether.","He was not a real doctor."],"k":1,"ty":"inference","e":"He did not publish until years later.","h":"تأخر في النشر."},{"n":16,"s":"Why was chloroform preferred to ether at first?","o":["It was easier to use and did not catch fire.","It was cheaper and safer for the heart.","It smelled more pleasant and lasted longer.","It was used by Ibn Sina."],"k":0,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Ether had an unpleasant smell and could catch fire.","h":"أسهل وغير قابل للاشتعال."},{"n":17,"s":"Why does the writer mention Queen Victoria?","o":["to show how chloroform became widely accepted","to explain why chloroform was dangerous","to describe a famous operation","to show that she was a doctor"],"k":0,"ty":"purpose","e":"It was widely accepted after she used it.","h":"لبيان انتشار قبوله."},{"n":18,"s":"According to paragraph 5, how did anaesthesia change surgery?","o":["Surgeons had to work faster.","Fewer operations were carried out.","Surgeons could perform longer and more complex operations.","Infections increased."],"k":2,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Paragraph 5 explains this.","h":"عمليات أطول وأعقد."},{"n":19,"s":"The word 'numb' in paragraph 6 is closest in meaning to","o":["heat","clean","wake up","remove feeling from"],"k":3,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"Local anaesthetics remove feeling from a small area.","h":"يخدّر."},{"n":20,"s":"How is the passage mainly organized?","o":["chronologically, from early pain relief to modern practice","as a comparison of two doctors","as a list of arguments","as a description of one operation"],"k":0,"ty":"organization","e":"Ancient → 1840s → chloroform → modern.","h":"ترتيب زمني."}]},{"t":"Ant colonies and teamwork","p":["A single ant is a tiny creature with a very small brain. On its own, it can do very little. Yet ant colonies, which may contain millions of individuals, are capable of extraordinary achievements: building complex nests, finding food efficiently, defending their territory and even farming. Scientists who study ants are fascinated by how such impressive results can arise without any leader giving orders.","An ant colony is usually built around one or more queens, whose main job is to lay eggs. Despite her name, the queen does not control the colony. Most of the ants are female workers, which carry out different tasks depending on their age and the needs of the colony. Young workers often stay inside the nest, caring for eggs and larvae, while older workers go outside to search for food and defend the nest.","One of the keys to the colony's success is communication through chemicals called pheromones. When a worker finds food, it returns to the nest, leaving a trail of pheromones behind it. Other ants follow the trail to the food and add more pheromones on their way back. If the food source is rich, the trail becomes stronger as more ants use it. When the food runs out, ants stop adding pheromones, and the trail slowly disappears. In this way, the colony can quickly direct its workers to the best food sources without any single ant understanding the whole situation.","Scientists call this kind of behaviour 'swarm intelligence': intelligent group behaviour that emerges from simple individual actions. Ant colonies can solve surprisingly difficult problems. For example, experiments have shown that ants can find the shortest route between their nest and a food source. Engineers and computer scientists have used these ideas to design systems that plan delivery routes, manage communication networks and control groups of small robots.","Some ant species show remarkable forms of cooperation. Leafcutter ants in Central and South America cut pieces of leaves and carry them back to their nests, but they do not eat the leaves. Instead, they use them to grow a special fungus, which they eat. Army ants in tropical forests have no permanent nest; when they rest, thousands of workers link their bodies together to form a living shelter that protects the queen and young.","Ants have existed for more than one hundred million years and live on every continent except Antarctica. Their success shows how cooperation and simple rules can produce complex and effective societies, a lesson that has inspired scientists, engineers and even business managers."],"q":[{"n":21,"s":"What fascinates scientists about ant colonies?","o":["Ants have very large brains.","Each ant works completely alone.","Queens control every ant.","They achieve impressive results without a leader giving orders."],"k":3,"ty":"main idea","e":"Paragraph 1 states this.","h":"إنجازات دون قائد."},{"n":22,"s":"According to paragraph 2, what is the queen's main job?","o":["giving orders","laying eggs","finding food","defending the nest"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"'whose main job is to lay eggs'.","h":"وضع البيض."},{"n":23,"s":"How are tasks usually divided among workers?","o":["by the queen's choice","according to their size only","according to their age and the colony's needs","randomly each day"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 2 explains this.","h":"حسب العمر والحاجة."},{"n":24,"s":"What happens to a pheromone trail when food runs out?","o":["It becomes stronger.","It changes colour.","It slowly disappears.","It leads to the queen."],"k":2,"ty":"sequence","e":"Ants stop adding pheromones.","h":"يتلاشى."},{"n":25,"s":"The phrase 'swarm intelligence' refers to","o":["intelligent group behaviour arising from simple individual actions","the intelligence of a single ant","a type of computer","the queen's ability to plan"],"k":0,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"Paragraph 4 defines it.","h":"ذكاء جماعي."},{"n":26,"s":"Why does the writer mention delivery routes and robots?","o":["to explain how ants travel","to show how ideas from ants have been applied by humans","to describe a type of ant","to criticize engineers"],"k":1,"ty":"purpose","e":"Engineers used ant ideas.","h":"تطبيقات بشرية."},{"n":27,"s":"What do leafcutter ants use leaves for?","o":["to build their nests","to eat directly","to grow fungus that they eat","to feed the queen"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 5 explains this.","h":"زراعة الفطر."},{"n":28,"s":"What is unusual about army ants?","o":["They live only in Antarctica.","Workers link their bodies to form a living shelter.","They have no queen.","They farm fungus."],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 5 describes this.","h":"مأوى حي من أجسادها."},{"n":29,"s":"Which statement best paraphrases 'The colony can quickly direct its workers to the best food sources without any single ant understanding the whole situation'?","o":["The group finds good food efficiently even though no ant knows everything.","Each ant understands where all the food is.","The queen tells workers where to go.","Ants find food slowly because they lack information."],"k":0,"ty":"paraphrase","e":"Same meaning, different words.","h":"إعادة صياغة صحيحة."},{"n":30,"s":"What is the main lesson the writer draws from ants?","o":["Large brains are necessary for success.","Leaders are always essential.","Insects are dangerous to humans.","Cooperation and simple rules can create complex, effective societies."],"k":3,"ty":"summary / conclusion","e":"The last paragraph states this.","h":"التعاون والقواعد البسيطة."}]},{"t":"Saving the Arabian leopard","p":["The Arabian leopard is the smallest leopard subspecies in the world, but it is a powerful and beautiful hunter. It has a pale golden coat covered with dark rosettes, long legs and a long tail that helps it keep its balance on steep rocks. Once found across the mountains of the Arabian Peninsula, from the Hijaz to Yemen and Oman, it is now critically endangered. Experts believe that fewer than two hundred remain in the wild.","Several factors have led to the leopard's decline. As human settlements, roads and farms expanded, much of its mountain habitat was lost or divided into small areas. At the same time, the populations of its natural prey, such as the Nubian ibex, hyraxes and gazelles, fell because of hunting and competition with domestic animals. With less wild prey available, some leopards attacked goats and sheep, and they were killed by farmers protecting their animals. In addition, leopards were sometimes captured and sold illegally.","Today, the Arabian leopard survives mainly in remote mountain areas of Oman and Yemen, and possibly in small numbers in Saudi Arabia. Because the animals are shy, nocturnal and live in difficult terrain, they are very hard to study. Researchers use camera traps, cameras that take photographs automatically when an animal passes, to identify individual leopards by the unique pattern of spots on their coats.","Saudi Arabia has made the Arabian leopard a national conservation priority. The Royal Commission for AlUla has established a breeding programme that has successfully increased the number of leopards in captivity, with the long-term aim of reintroducing them into the wild. Before this can happen, however, conservationists must ensure that there is enough protected habitat and sufficient wild prey. Projects are therefore also protecting and reintroducing species such as the ibex and the gazelle.","Working with local communities is essential. Conservationists explain the importance of leopards to the ecosystem and work with farmers to reduce conflicts, for example by building stronger enclosures for livestock at night. Some programmes compensate farmers for animals lost to predators, so that they are less likely to harm leopards. Awareness campaigns also encourage pride in the leopard as a symbol of Arabia's natural heritage. In 2023, the United Nations declared 10 February as International Day of the Arabian Leopard.","The future of the Arabian leopard is uncertain, but there is reason for hope. The successful return of the Arabian oryx to the wild shows that, with long-term commitment and cooperation, even critically endangered species can recover."],"q":[{"n":31,"s":"Why is the Arabian leopard described as critically endangered?","o":["It is the smallest leopard.","Fewer than two hundred remain in the wild.","It lives only in zoos.","It has a golden coat."],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 1 states this.","h":"أقل من مئتين في البرية."},{"n":32,"s":"What helps the leopard keep its balance on steep rocks?","o":["its pale coat","its dark rosettes","its long tail","its small size"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph 1 explains this.","h":"ذيله الطويل."},{"n":33,"s":"Why did some leopards attack goats and sheep?","o":["They preferred domestic animals.","Their wild prey had become scarce.","Farmers fed them.","They were trained to hunt."],"k":1,"ty":"cause–effect","e":"Less wild prey was available.","h":"قلة الفرائس البرية."},{"n":34,"s":"Which of the following is NOT given as a cause of the leopard's decline?","o":["habitat loss","a decline in prey","illegal capture and sale","disease spread by tourists"],"k":3,"ty":"NOT / EXCEPT","e":"Tourist disease is not mentioned.","h":"المرض غير مذكور."},{"n":35,"s":"What are camera traps used for?","o":["catching leopards for zoos","scaring leopards away from farms","identifying individual leopards","counting tourists"],"k":2,"ty":"purpose","e":"They identify leopards by their spots.","h":"التعرف على النمور."},{"n":36,"s":"Why must conservationists protect prey species before reintroducing leopards?","o":["Prey species are more valuable.","Leopards cannot hunt.","Leopards need enough wild food to survive.","Tourists prefer to see ibex."],"k":2,"ty":"inference","e":"There must be sufficient wild prey.","h":"يحتاج النمر غذاءً كافيًا."},{"n":37,"s":"The word 'compensate' in paragraph 5 is closest in meaning to","o":["punish","train","warn","pay for a loss"],"k":3,"ty":"vocabulary in context","e":"Programmes pay farmers for lost animals.","h":"يعوّض."},{"n":38,"s":"What is the purpose of paragraph 5?","o":["to describe the leopard's appearance","to explain the history of AlUla","to explain the role of local communities in conservation","to compare leopards and oryx"],"k":2,"ty":"insertion / paragraph function","e":"It describes working with farmers and awareness.","h":"دور المجتمع المحلي."},{"n":39,"s":"Why does the writer mention the Arabian oryx at the end?","o":["as evidence that endangered species can recover","to show that oryx are leopards' prey","to compare their coats","to describe a failed project"],"k":0,"ty":"purpose","e":"Its return shows recovery is possible.","h":"دليل على إمكان التعافي."},{"n":40,"s":"What is the writer's attitude towards the leopard's future?","o":["cautiously hopeful","completely pessimistic","indifferent","certain of success"],"k":0,"ty":"attitude / tone","e":"'uncertain, but there is reason for hope'.","h":"متفائل بحذر."}]}],"i":"Read each passage and answer the questions that follow. Choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","iar":"اقرأ كل نص ثم أجب عن الأسئلة التي تليه، واختر الإجابة الصحيحة."},{"id":"S","name":"Sentence Structure","ar":"تركيب الجمل","min":35,"from":41,"to":70,"g":[{"i":"Choose the word or phrase that best completes the sentence.","err":false,"q":[{"n":41,"s":"We ______ in this apartment since January, but we still haven't unpacked everything.","o":["are living","live","were living","have lived"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"have lived — since + present perfect for a situation continuing to now.","h":"المضارع التام مع since."},{"n":42,"s":"The results of the experiment ______ in a scientific journal next year.","o":["will be published","will publish","publish","are publishing"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"will be published — Future passive.","h":"المبني للمجهول."},{"n":43,"s":"______ you have any questions, please contact the office.","o":["Would","Had","Should","Were"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"Should — Inverted conditional: Should you …","h":"شرط مقلوب."},{"n":44,"s":"The town ______ my grandfather was born has changed completely.","o":["which","where","whose","that's"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"where — where for places.","h":"where."},{"n":45,"s":"If the bus ______ on time, we wouldn't have missed the start of the film.","o":["came","had come","would come","has come"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"had come — Third conditional.","h":"الشرط الثالث."},{"n":46,"s":"My brother is considering ______ engineering at university.","o":["studying","to study","study","studied"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"studying — consider + -ing.","h":"consider + -ing."},{"n":47,"s":"We had the old carpets ______ and new ones fitted.","o":["remove","removing","removed","to remove"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"removed — Causative.","h":"التركيب السببي."},{"n":48,"s":"The ______ we waited, the angrier the passengers became.","o":["longer","longest","more long","long"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"longer — the + comparative, the + comparative.","h":"كلما … كلما."},{"n":49,"s":"You ______ have told me you were coming! I would have cooked something special.","o":["must","can't","would","should"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"should — Criticism of a past action: should have.","h":"should have للوم."},{"n":50,"s":"If only I ______ my passport at home. Now I can't check in.","o":["hadn't left","didn't leave","haven't left","wouldn't leave"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"hadn't left — Past regret.","h":"ندم على الماضي."},{"n":51,"s":"By the time you read this letter, I ______ for London.","o":["will have left","will leave","leave","am leaving"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"will have left — Future perfect.","h":"المستقبل التام."},{"n":52,"s":"She advised me ______ my CV before applying.","o":["updating","update","to update","that update"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"to update — advise + object + to + verb.","h":"advise + to."},{"n":53,"s":"______ of the bad weather, the flight left on time.","o":["In spite","Despite","Although","Even"],"k":0,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"In spite — In spite of + noun.","h":"In spite of."},{"n":54,"s":"I've had ______ problems with this car that I'm going to sell it.","o":["such","so many","so much","too many that"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"so many — so many + countable noun + that.","h":"so many."},{"n":55,"s":"The police ______ looking for two men in connection with the robbery.","o":["is","has","was","are"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"are — police takes a plural verb.","h":"police جمع."},{"n":56,"s":"In the past, people ______ travel for weeks to reach Makkah.","o":["were","would","used","are used to"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"would — would for repeated past actions.","h":"would للعادة."},{"n":57,"s":"My uncle, ______ company builds bridges, has just won an award.","o":["who's","which","whose","that"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"whose — whose for possession in a non-defining clause.","h":"whose."},{"n":58,"s":"Little ______ that the surprise party was for him.","o":["he knew","did he know","he did know","knew he"],"k":1,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"did he know — Negative adverbial at the start: inversion.","h":"القلب بعد Little."},{"n":59,"s":"I can't afford ______ a new laptop this year.","o":["buying","buy","to buy","bought"],"k":2,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"to buy — afford + to + verb.","h":"afford + to."},{"n":60,"s":"Were I in your position, I ______ the job offer.","o":["will accept","accepted","would have accept","would accept"],"k":3,"ty":"sentence completion","e":"would accept — Inverted second conditional.","h":"شرط ثانٍ مقلوب."}]},{"i":"Choose the underlined part (A, B, C or D) that is incorrect.","err":true,"q":[{"n":61,"s":"The price of houses (A) in the city (B) has risen (C) sharply (D) since five years.","o":["in","has","sharply","since five years"],"k":3,"ty":"error identification","e":"since five years — A period up to now: in the last five years / for five years.","h":"for five years."},{"n":62,"s":"(A) Despite of the cost, (B) many families (C) bought (D) electric cars.","o":["Despite of","many","bought","electric"],"k":0,"ty":"error identification","e":"Despite of — despite takes no of.","h":"despite بلا of."},{"n":63,"s":"If I (A) had (B) known the answer, I (C) would tell you (D) yesterday.","o":["had","known","would tell","yesterday"],"k":2,"ty":"error identification","e":"would tell — Third conditional: would have told.","h":"would have told."},{"n":64,"s":"She (A) avoided (B) to look at the (C) exam results (D) until the evening.","o":["avoided","to look","exam","until"],"k":1,"ty":"error identification","e":"to look — avoid + -ing: looking.","h":"avoid + -ing."},{"n":65,"s":"The man (A) who (B) I (C) met him at the conference (D) works for a bank.","o":["who","I","met him","works"],"k":2,"ty":"error identification","e":"met him — him repeats the object of who: I met.","h":"لا نكرر الضمير."},{"n":66,"s":"He (A) must (B) have (C) been tired after (D) drive all night.","o":["must","have","been","drive"],"k":3,"ty":"error identification","e":"drive — after + -ing: driving.","h":"بعد after يأتي -ing."},{"n":67,"s":"Each of the (A) players (B) were given (C) a new (D) shirt.","o":["players","were","a","shirt"],"k":1,"ty":"error identification","e":"were — Each of … takes a singular verb: was.","h":"Each مفرد."},{"n":68,"s":"Hardly (A) I had arrived (B) when it (C) started (D) to rain.","o":["I had","when","started","to rain"],"k":0,"ty":"error identification","e":"I had — Inversion after Hardly: had I.","h":"القلب: had I."},{"n":69,"s":"The report (A) needs (B) to be (C) finished (D) until Thursday.","o":["needs","to be","finished","until"],"k":3,"ty":"error identification","e":"until — A deadline uses by: by Thursday.","h":"by للموعد النهائي."},{"n":70,"s":"I (A) would rather you (B) didn't (C) told anyone (D) about this.","o":["would","didn't","told","about"],"k":2,"ty":"error identification","e":"told — didn't + base verb: didn't tell.","h":"didn't مع المصدر."}]}],"iar":"الأسئلة من ٤١ إلى ٦٠: اختر الكلمة أو العبارة التي تكمل الجملة إكمالًا صحيحًا."},{"id":"L","name":"Listening Comprehension","ar":"فهم المسموع","min":30,"from":71,"to":90,"g":[{"rec":1,"a":"M15-L-01","q":[{"n":71,"s":"What will happen if there is a leak?","o":["The repair could take two days.","The repair will take thirty minutes.","The man will need a new car.","The mechanic will refuse to repair it."],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"'If there's a leak, I'll need to order a part, and that could take two days.'","h":"يومان."}],"t":"A broken air-conditioner in a car","sc":["Situation: A man is speaking to a mechanic at a garage. (71 words)","Man: The air conditioner in my car is only blowing warm air. In this heat, I can't drive like this.","Man: It's probably low on gas. That's a common problem in summer. I can check it now.","Man: How long will it take?","Man: If it's just the gas, about thirty minutes. If there's a leak, I'll need to order a part, and that could take two days.","Man: Let's hope it's just the gas, then."]},{"rec":2,"a":"M15-L-02","q":[{"n":72,"s":"What is the main problem with the student's essay?","o":["Her ideas are weak.","Her spelling is poor.","Her paragraphs contain too many different points.","Her essay is too short."],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"'each one contains several different points'.","h":"الفقرات تحوي أفكارًا كثيرة."}],"t":"Asking for feedback on an essay","sc":["Situation: A student speaks to her English teacher after class. (57 words)","Woman: Ms. Sarah, could you tell me how I can improve my essay? I got a seventy.","Woman: Your ideas are good, but your paragraphs are too long, and each one contains several different points.","Woman: So I should divide them?","Woman: Exactly. Give each paragraph one main idea with a clear topic sentence, and your mark will improve a lot."]},{"rec":3,"a":"M15-L-03","q":[{"n":73,"s":"Why do the tickets show the wrong date?","o":["The theatre made a printing error.","The show was moved to another day.","The website was not working.","The customer chose the wrong date when booking."],"k":3,"ty":"reason","e":"'You selected the wrong date when you booked.'","h":"اختار التاريخ الخطأ."}],"t":"A ticket for the wrong date","sc":["Situation: A customer speaks to an employee at a theatre box office. (70 words)","Man: Excuse me, I bought tickets online for tonight's show, but these say tomorrow's date.","Woman: Let me check your booking. I see. You selected the wrong date when you booked.","Man: Oh no. Is there any way to change them? We can't come tomorrow.","Woman: Tonight's show is almost full, but there are two seats in the balcony. I can exchange them for a small fee of twenty riyals.","Man: That's fine. Thank you."]},{"rec":4,"a":"M15-L-04","q":[{"n":74,"s":"Why was Huda able to visit?","o":["She lives nearby.","Her flight was cancelled.","Her training course ended early.","She was invited for lunch."],"k":2,"ty":"reason","e":"'I finished my training course two days early'.","h":"انتهت الدورة مبكرًا."}],"t":"A friend's surprise visit","sc":["Situation: Two friends meet unexpectedly at a door. (55 words)","Woman: Huda! What a surprise! I thought you were still in Riyadh.","Woman: I finished my training course two days early, so I decided to visit before going home.","Woman: I'm so happy to see you. Come in. Have you had lunch?","Woman: Not yet, but I don't want to cause any trouble. I just wanted to say hello."]},{"rec":5,"a":"M15-L-05","q":[{"n":75,"s":"When will the man use the sports hall?","o":["on Sunday evening","on Saturday evening","on Saturday morning","on Monday evening"],"k":0,"ty":"correction","e":"Saturday is booked; he accepts Sunday from six to eight.","h":"الأحد مساءً."}],"t":"Booking a sports hall","sc":["Situation: A man calls a sports centre. (56 words)","Man: Hello. I'd like to book the sports hall for a basketball game this Saturday evening.","Woman: I'm sorry, the hall is booked for a volleyball tournament all day Saturday. It's free on Sunday from six to eight, though.","Man: Sunday is fine. How much is it for two hours?","Woman: Three hundred riyals. You can pay when you arrive."]},{"rec":6,"a":"M15-L-06","q":[{"n":76,"s":"What does the man suggest?","o":["telling the manager immediately","talking to Majed before involving the manager","starting meetings without Majed","ignoring the problem"],"k":1,"ty":"function","e":"'I think we should talk to him first.'","h":"التحدث معه أولًا."}],"t":"A colleague who is always late","sc":["Situation: Two colleagues are talking in an office. (50 words)","Woman: Majed was late for the meeting again today. That's the fourth time this month.","Man: I know. It's affecting the whole team, because we can't start without his figures.","Woman: Should we tell the manager?","Man: I think we should talk to him first. Maybe he has a problem we don't know about."]},{"rec":7,"a":"M15-L-07","q":[{"n":77,"s":"When does the pharmacist recommend taking the tablets?","o":["in the morning","before driving","with lunch","at night, before going to bed"],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"'It's better to take them at night'.","h":"ليلًا قبل النوم."}],"t":"Asking a pharmacist about side effects","sc":["Situation: A woman speaks to a pharmacist. (57 words)","Woman: The doctor gave me these tablets for my allergy. Are there any side effects?","Man: They can make some people feel sleepy, so you shouldn't drive after taking them until you know how they affect you.","Woman: Should I take them in the morning or at night?","Man: It's better to take them at night, before you go to bed."]},{"rec":8,"a":"M15-L-08","q":[{"n":78,"s":"How will the company find the driver?","o":["by checking the car number","by asking at the airport","by using the record of the card payment","by calling the man's phone Longer conversations"],"k":2,"ty":"detail","e":"He paid by card, so there is a record.","h":"من سجل الدفع."}],"t":"A dropped phone in a taxi","sc":["Situation: A man calls a taxi company. (70 words)","Man: Hello. I took one of your taxis from the airport about an hour ago, and I think I left my phone on the back seat.","Woman: Do you remember the car number or the driver's name?","Man: No, but I paid by card, so you should have a record of the journey.","Woman: Yes, I can find it. I'll contact the driver and call you back on this number in a few minutes."]},{"rec":9,"a":"M15-L-09","q":[{"n":79,"s":"Why can the students enter only the visitors' area?","o":["because the plant is closed","for safety reasons","because it is too small","because the engineers are busy"],"k":1,"ty":"reason","e":"'Only in the visitors' area, for safety reasons.'","h":"للسلامة."},{"n":80,"s":"Why will each group prepare questions?","o":["because the engineers asked for them","because they will be tested","to make the visit more useful","to save time on the bus"],"k":2,"ty":"purpose","e":"'That way, the visit will be more useful.'","h":"لجعل الزيارة مفيدة."}],"t":"Planning a field trip to a desalination plant","sc":["Situation: A science teacher and a student leader are planning a trip. (144 words)","Man: Our class has permission to visit the desalination plant in Jubail next month. Can you help me prepare?","Man: Sure, I'd be happy to. What exactly will we see there?","Man: The engineers will show us how sea water is turned into drinking water using reverse osmosis, where water is pushed through very fine filters.","Man: Will we be allowed inside the plant?","Man: Only in the visitors' area, for safety reasons. We'll need to wear helmets and closed shoes.","Man: I'll remind everyone about the shoes. What should students prepare beforehand?","Man: I'd like each group to prepare three questions for the engineers. That way, the visit will be more useful.","Man: Good idea. I'll collect the questions by next Wednesday so you can check them.","Man: Excellent. And please also ask who needs a packed lunch, because we won't be back until three. The school will provide water for everyone."]},{"rec":10,"a":"M15-L-10","q":[{"n":81,"s":"Why is the first student voting for Rana?","o":["Rana is her best friend.","The school needs more clubs.","The canteen is still very bad.","Rana promised free lunches."],"k":1,"ty":"reason","e":"The canteen has improved, but there are only three clubs.","h":"حاجة لنوادٍ أكثر."},{"n":82,"s":"What will the second student do before deciding?","o":["ask her teacher","vote for Lama","start a study club","read the candidates' posters again"],"k":3,"ty":"detail","e":"'I'll read both of their posters again this evening'.","h":"تقرأ الملصقات."}],"t":"Discussing a student council election","sc":["Situation: Two students talk about the school council election. (142 words)","Woman: Are you going to vote in the student council election tomorrow?","Woman: Yes, but I haven't decided who to vote for. Lama wants to improve the canteen, and Rana wants to start more clubs.","Woman: I'm voting for Rana. The canteen has already improved a lot this year, but we only have three clubs.","Woman: That's true. But Lama also promised to organize study sessions before exams.","Woman: Rana said the clubs could include a study club, so that's covered too.","Woman: Then maybe Rana's plan is more complete. I'll read both of their posters again this evening before I decide.","Woman: Good idea. The most important thing is that everyone votes, whoever they choose. Last year, fewer than half of the students voted, and many of them complained afterwards.","Woman: That's true. If we want changes, we have to take part. I'll remind my friends to vote too."]},{"rec":11,"a":"M15-L-11","q":[{"n":83,"s":"What will the students' project test?","o":["how hot drinks become in the sun","which materials keep drinks cold longest","which drinks are healthiest","how to make a thermometer"],"k":1,"ty":"main idea","e":"They will test materials that keep drinks cold.","h":"المواد التي تحفظ البرودة."},{"n":84,"s":"Why do they want to repeat the test?","o":["because the first test failed","because the teacher requires three tests","to check their results","to use more materials Talks and lectures"],"k":2,"ty":"purpose","e":"'Let's also repeat the test twice to check our results.'","h":"للتحقق من النتائج."}],"t":"Choosing a topic for a science fair","sc":["Situation: Two students are choosing a science fair project. (153 words)","Man: We need a topic for the science fair. Any ideas?","Man: What about testing which materials keep drinks cold for the longest time? It's useful in our hot weather.","Man: I like that. We could test cardboard, foam, wool and aluminium foil.","Man: We'd need to make sure the test is fair. Every container should have the same amount of water at the same starting temperature.","Man: And we should measure the temperature every fifteen minutes for three hours.","Man: I have a digital thermometer at home. We can do the experiment in my garage at the weekend.","Man: Great. I'll make the graph and the poster afterwards. Let's also repeat the test twice to check our results.","Man: Good thinking. Scientists always repeat experiments. If our results are the same each time, the judges will trust them more. We could also add a fifth material, like newspaper, to see whether something cheap works well.","Man: Interesting idea. Let's add it."]},{"rec":12,"a":"M15-L-12","q":[{"n":85,"s":"What can a sudden increase in small earthquakes suggest?","o":["Magma may be moving towards the surface.","The volcano is becoming inactive.","The ground is cooling down.","Gas levels are falling."],"k":0,"ty":"detail","e":"Paragraph explains this sign.","h":"صعود الصهارة."},{"n":86,"s":"Why do scientists combine several methods?","o":["It is required by law.","Each method is very cheap.","Volcanoes erupt every year.","No single method is reliable on its own."],"k":3,"ty":"reason","e":"'No single method is reliable on its own'.","h":"لا طريقة موثوقة وحدها."},{"n":87,"s":"Why does the lecturer mention Mount Pinatubo?","o":["to describe the largest volcano in the world","to explain how gases are measured","to compare it with Harrat Rahat","to show how monitoring can save lives"],"k":3,"ty":"purpose of detail","e":"Monitoring allowed evacuation before the eruption.","h":"المراقبة تنقذ الأرواح."}],"t":"Lecture: how volcanoes are monitored","sc":["Situation: A geology lecturer is speaking to students. (254 words)","Lecturer: Good morning. Volcanic eruptions can be devastating, so scientists work hard to predict them. Although we cannot yet say exactly when a volcano will erupt, careful monitoring often gives us valuable warning signs. Today I'll describe the main methods. The first is measuring earthquakes. As magma rises beneath a volcano, it breaks rock and causes small earthquakes, often too weak for people to feel. Instruments called seismometers record these tremors. A sudden increase in the number of small earthquakes can mean that magma is moving towards the surface. The second method is measuring changes in the shape of the ground. When magma collects underground, the surface of the volcano may swell slightly, sometimes by only a few centimetres. Scientists use GPS instruments and satellite images to detect these tiny changes. The third method involves gases. As magma rises, it releases gases such as sulphur dioxide and carbon dioxide. An increase in these gases can suggest that an eruption is becoming more likely. Scientists measure gases using instruments on the ground and in aircraft. Finally, thermal cameras can detect rising temperatures on the surface. No single method is reliable on its own, so scientists combine all of this information. In 1991, monitoring of Mount Pinatubo in the Philippines allowed authorities to evacuate tens of thousands of people shortly before one of the largest eruptions of the twentieth century, saving many lives. Here in Saudi Arabia, the volcanic fields of Harrat Rahat near Madinah are also monitored, although no eruption is expected in the near future."]},{"rec":13,"a":"M15-L-13","q":[{"n":88,"s":"According to the counsellor, after how long does concentration usually drop?","o":["about ten minutes","about forty-five to sixty minutes","about two hours","about thirty seconds"],"k":1,"ty":"detail","e":"'our ability to concentrate drops after about forty-five to sixty minutes'.","h":"٤٥ إلى ٦٠ دقيقة."},{"n":89,"s":"Why does the counsellor advise against using social media during breaks?","o":["It does not really rest the brain.","It wastes phone battery.","It is not allowed at school.","It makes students hungry."],"k":0,"ty":"reason","e":"'this doesn't really rest the brain'.","h":"لا يريح الدماغ."},{"n":90,"s":"What does the counsellor say about staying up all night before an exam?","o":["It usually does more harm than good.","It helps students remember more.","It is the best way to revise.","It is necessary for difficult subjects."],"k":0,"ty":"opinion","e":"'Staying up all night … usually does more harm than good.'","h":"ضرره أكثر من نفعه."}],"t":"Talk: healthy study breaks","sc":["Situation: A school counsellor speaks to students before exams. (243 words)","Lecturer: Good morning, everyone. With exams starting in two weeks, many of you are studying for long hours. Today I want to talk about something that is just as important as studying: taking breaks. Research shows that our ability to concentrate drops after about forty-five to sixty minutes of focused work. If you keep going without a pause, you may spend more time but learn less. So, I recommend studying in blocks of about fifty minutes, followed by a ten-minute break. But what kind of break? Many students pick up their phones and scroll through social media. Unfortunately, this doesn't really rest the brain; it just fills it with more information. A better choice is to move your body. Stand up, stretch, walk around the house or step outside for some fresh air. Even a few minutes of light exercise increases blood flow to the brain and can improve your concentration when you return to your desk. Drink a glass of water, because even mild dehydration can make you feel tired. If you feel hungry, choose a healthy snack such as fruit or nuts instead of sweets, which give a quick burst of energy followed by tiredness. Finally, remember that sleep is the most important break of all. During sleep, your brain organizes and stores what you have learned. Staying up all night before an exam usually does more harm than good. Plan your time, take regular breaks and look after yourselves. Good luck!"]}],"i":"You will hear 13 recordings: 8 short conversations (one question each), 3 longer conversations (two questions each) and 2 talks (three questions each). Read the questions before each recording, then choose the best answer.","iar":"ستسمع ثلاثة عشر تسجيلًا: ثماني محادثات قصيرة (سؤال لكل منها)، وثلاث محادثات أطول (سؤالان لكل منها)، وحديثين أو محاضرتين (ثلاثة أسئلة لكل منهما). اقرأ الأسئلة قبل بدء كل تسجيل."},{"id":"C","name":"Composition Analysis","ar":"التحليل الإنشائي","min":20,"from":91,"to":100,"g":[{"q":[{"n":91,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 1","Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4"],"x":["(1) Desalination provides much of the drinking water in Saudi Arabia. (2) Sea water is pushed through special filters that remove salt. (3) The process uses large amounts of energy. (4) The Red Sea is famous for its colourful coral reefs. (5) Engineers are developing solar-powered plants to reduce energy costs."],"k":3,"ty":"irrelevant sentence","e":"Coral reefs are not about desalination.","h":"الشعاب خارج الموضوع."},{"n":92,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Some loans must be repaid quickly.","Entrepreneurship is becoming an important part of the Kingdom's economy.","Online customers often read reviews.","Training courses can be expensive."],"x":["Many young Saudis are now starting their own businesses. Government programmes offer training, loans and advice, and new technology makes it easier to reach customers online. Successful start-ups are also creating jobs for others. ______"],"k":1,"ty":"concluding sentence","e":"A conclusion that sums up the trend.","h":"خلاصة الاتجاه."},{"n":93,"s":"The research team (A) has (B) discovered that the new drug (C) reduce symptoms (D) significantly.","o":["has","discovered","reduce","significantly"],"k":2,"ty":"error","e":"the new drug is singular: reduces.","h":"reduces."},{"n":94,"s":"Which sentence does NOT belong in the paragraph?","o":["Sentence 2","Sentence 3","Sentence 4","Sentence 5"],"x":["(1) Learning to cook is a valuable life skill. (2) It allows people to eat healthier, cheaper meals. (3) It also encourages creativity and independence. (4) Many restaurants offer delivery services late at night. (5) Cooking for others can be a way of showing care."],"k":2,"ty":"irrelevant sentence","e":"Restaurant delivery does not support the value of learning to cook.","h":"التوصيل خارج الفكرة."},{"n":95,"s":"Choose the best order for the sentences.","o":["2 – 3 – 4 – 1","2 – 4 – 3 – 1","3 – 2 – 4 – 1","2 – 3 – 1 – 4"],"x":["(1) This has led to a sharp increase in visitors to the region.","(2) In recent years, AlUla has been transformed into a major cultural destination.","(3) Ancient sites such as Hegra have been opened to the public.","(4) Festivals, concerts and art exhibitions are also held there throughout the year."],"k":0,"ty":"best order","e":"topic → sites → also events → This has led to.","h":"تسلسل منطقي."},{"n":96,"s":"Which sentence is the best topic sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Birds build nests in spring.","Planting trees in cities brings many environmental benefits.","Some streets are very narrow.","Pollution comes from cars and factories."],"x":["______ Trees provide shade, which lowers temperatures in streets. They also absorb pollution and give birds and insects a place to live."],"k":1,"ty":"topic sentence / thesis","e":"The details list benefits of urban trees.","h":"فوائد الأشجار في المدن."},{"n":97,"s":"Which sentence is the best concluding sentence for the paragraph?","o":["Some children's books are expensive.","Many children enjoy cartoons.","Libraries close early on Fridays.","Parents should therefore make reading a daily habit with their children."],"x":["Reading to young children has many advantages. It builds their vocabulary, develops their imagination and helps them understand the world. It also creates special moments between parents and children. ______"],"k":3,"ty":"concluding sentence","e":"A recommendation drawn from the advantages.","h":"توصية."},{"n":98,"s":"Which word or phrase best fills the blank?","o":["On the other hand","As a result","For instance","Furthermore"],"x":["Some people prefer to live in big cities because of the job opportunities. ______, others choose small towns for their peace and quiet."],"k":0,"ty":"transition / connector","e":"Contrasting preferences.","h":"تضاد."},{"n":99,"s":"Hardly (A) anyone (B) came to the meeting, (C) so it (D) cancelled.","o":["anyone","came","so","cancelled"],"k":3,"ty":"error","e":"Passive is needed: it was cancelled.","h":"المبني للمجهول."},{"n":100,"s":"Which sentence best fills the blank in the paragraph?","o":["Deserts receive very little rain.","Every household can take simple steps to save water.","Some gardens have many flowers.","Showers are more popular than baths. Teacher Section — Mock 15"],"x":["Water conservation is especially important in desert countries. ______ For example, they can repair leaking taps, take shorter showers and water gardens at night."],"k":1,"ty":"complete the paragraph","e":"For example needs a general statement about households.","h":"عبارة عامة قبل المثال."}]}],"i":"Read each paragraph or set of sentences and choose the best answer (A, B, C or D).","iar":"اقرأ كل فقرة أو مجموعة جمل واختر الإجابة الصحيحة."}]};
